ess; a field that has none cannot violate it. One cross-field interlock spans","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"both groups and is checked on the resolved policy rather than on either input: see","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"validate_dcr_policy","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"].","type":"text"}],"title":"OidcPolicy","kind":"symbol"},"doc://AxiamSDK/s8SendableP":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP","title":"Swift.Sendable"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/externalClientAllowedResources":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"externalClientAllowedResources","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"]?","kind":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/externalClientAllowedResources","kind":"symbol","title":"externalClientAllowedResources","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/externalclientallowedresources","abstract":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"D3","type":"text"}]},{"text":" — the audiences an externally registered client may address. The single most","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"important field on this policy, and the reason the settings handler refuses"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dynamic_registration: anonymous"},{"type":"text","text":" while it is empty. A client an unrelated party"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"registered cannot declare its own ","type":"text"},{"code":"allowed_resources","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; it inherits this list verbatim,"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"so what a stranger can mint a token ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"for","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is a decision the tenant took in advance"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"rather than one the registration request makes. Empty means an externally registered","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"client can obtain only today’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"axiam:user","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" tokens — which AXIAM’s own APIs accept. That"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"is why the interlock exists: the empty list is not a safe default for an ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"open","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registration endpoint, it is the most dangerous one. Shared with T5 (CIMD), which"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inherits the same list for the same reason."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/encode(to:)":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/encode(to:)","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/encode(to:)","title":"encode(to:)","role":"symbol","abstract":[],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"encode","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"to","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s7EncoderP","text":"Encoder","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/dynamicRegistration":{"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/dynamicregistration","abstract":[{"text":"T21.4 — whether a client may register itself (RFC 7591), and on what terms. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"disabled"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unless somebody says otherwise (I1).","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dynamicRegistration","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dynamicRegistration","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"title":"dynamicRegistration"},"doc://AxiamSDK/SE":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/SE","title":"Swift.Encodable"},"doc://AxiamSDK/Se":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/Se","title":"Swift.Decodable"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk","role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK","kind":"symbol","title":"AxiamSDK","abstract":[{"text":"The official Swift SDK for AXIAM (Access eXtended Identity and Authorization Management).","type":"text"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/cimd":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/cimd","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/cimd","title":"cimd","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"T21.5 — whether a URL-shaped "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"client_id"},{"type":"text","text":" is resolved by fetching the document it names,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and on what terms. See ["},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"CimdPolicy"},{"type":"text","text":"]; off unless somebody turns it on (I1). Nested, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"therefore inherited or overridden "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"whole"}]},{"type":"text","text":": the fields are terms of one decision, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"half-merged posture is one neither the organization nor the tenant wrote."}],"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"cimd","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"CimdPolicy","preciseIdentifier":"s:8AxiamSDK10CimdPolicyV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/sensitiveScopesEnabled":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/sensitiveScopesEnabled","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/sensitivescopesenabled","title":"sensitiveScopesEnabled","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Whether "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"address"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"phone"},{"type":"text","text":" may be registered on a client, requested at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"authorization endpoint, and released at UserInfo (X7 G8). "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Off unless an organization"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"turns it on."}]},{"type":"text","text":" The two scopes release a postal address and a telephone number —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"categories of personal data AXIAM has no other use for — so the deployment that has"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never thought about them releases nothing, and the operator who has thought about them"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"says so once, at the organization level, where the lawful basis for holding the data was","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"decided. The switch is a ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"capability"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"text":", not a grant: with it on, a client still has to","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"register the scope, the request still has to ask for it, and the user still has to have","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consented. It is the first of four gates, and it is the only one an operator can close","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"for everybody at once.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"sensitiveScopesEnabled"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}]},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/dcrUnusedClientTTLDays":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dcrUnusedClientTTLDays"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/dcrunusedclientttldays","title":"dcrUnusedClientTTLDays","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"T21.4 — how long an externally registered client survives without being used. See"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"["},{"code":"DEFAULT_DCR_UNUSED_CLIENT_TTL_DAYS","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"]. "},{"code":"0","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" disables the sweep for this tenant, which an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"operator who prunes out of band may legitimately want. "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Two sweeps read it, over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"different clocks","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" (T21.8). A "},{"code":"managed_by: dcr","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" row is measured from its last"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"authorization, falling back to when it was registered. A ","type":"text"},{"code":"managed_by: cimd","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" row is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"measured from the last time its document was "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"presented"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":", which every authorize, token"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and PAR request moves — so a document in daily use is never swept however old its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registration is, and one nobody has presented since the window is, and re-materialises"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on the next request if it is still published. Like the ceiling, it keeps its "},{"code":"dcr_","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"name."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dcrUnusedClientTTLDays","type":"topic"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/init(from:)":{"title":"init(from:)","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/init(from:)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"init","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"from","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": any ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Decoder","preciseIdentifier":"s:s7DecoderP","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/init(from:)","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/dcrMaxClients":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dcrMaxClients","abstract":[{"text":"T21.4 — how many externally registered clients this tenant may hold. See","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"DEFAULT_DCR_MAX_CLIENTS","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"]. ","type":"text"},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Counted once per mechanism, against the same number","type":"text"}]},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(T21.8): ","type":"text"},{"code":"managed_by: dcr","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" rows and ","type":"text"},{"code":"managed_by: cimd","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" rows each have this many. So a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tenant running both cannot have shadow rows materialised from documents exhaust the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"allowance for self-registration, or the reverse. The CIMD count is checked ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"before","type":"text"}]},{"text":" the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"document is fetched, so a tenant at its ceiling is not an outbound amplifier either. It","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps its ","type":"text"},{"code":"dcr_","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" name because dynamic registration defined it, on the same precedent as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"[","type":"text"},{"code":"Self::dcr_allowed_scopes","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"].","type":"text"}],"title":"dcrMaxClients","url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/dcrmaxclients","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"dcrMaxClients","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://AxiamSDK/documentation/AxiamSDK/OidcPolicy/dcrAllowedRedirectHosts":{"title":"dcrAllowedRedirectHosts","abstract":[{"text":"T21.4 — hosts a self-registered client’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"redirect_uris","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" may point at, as globs","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(","type":"text"},{"code":"*.example.com","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", or ","type":"text"},{"code":"*","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for any). The loopback hosts (","type":"text"},{"code":"127.0.0.1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"[::1]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"localhost","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") are always allowed whatever this says, because RFC 8252 §7.3 is how every","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"desktop MCP client receives its callback and a tenant that forbade them would have","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"turned registration on for nobody.","type":"text"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/OidcPolicy\/dcrAllowedRedirectHosts","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"dcrAllowedRedirectHosts"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"]?","kind":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/oidcpolicy\/dcrallowedredirecthosts","role":"symbol","type":"topic"}}}